ry":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-k3[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Album notes — every record collection hangs under the area it [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]serves[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every record note reaches an area of responsibility. Each record [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]collection (eat, podcasts, tv, movies) becomes an album note: [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`type: \"[\\[album]]\"` under its owner area, holding its record schema[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]in frontmatter instead of `config.yml`, de-zorged, and showing a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]generated, grouped `[!records]` index. Every owner area or project [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]shows a beautiful generated `## Albums` catalog. Records become [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`type: \"[\\[record]]\"` children of their album. Schema and data [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]version together in the vault, a broken album fails alone, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]glossary terms for album note and record note are published.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]11[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]album_and_record_notes.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/album_and_record_notes.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-k3[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-k3/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Vault-only cleanup — owners, the eat.md de-zorg, and record [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]health[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]vault-cleanup[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault-cleanup: with today's bob and no code, point eat at body, podcasts[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]at dev, and tv at fun; de-zorg eat.md into a legacy_eat notebook under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]body after carrying footnote 17; rewrite the mapped block links; strip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`companions`; fill the six empty categories; fold the location [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]spellings; and gate on zero `bob records check` findings and no new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]broken links.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Album recognition, the vault schema registry, and bob albums [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]list and check[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]album-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]album-model: recognize `type: \"[\\[album]]\"` and `type: \"[\\[record]]\"`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parse album frontmatter (top-level facts plus one nested `record:` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]schema) with key-path and line diagnostics, build the vault-aware [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record-kind registry with per-album isolation and the album-wins [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]transition rule over config, and ship the read-only `bob albums list` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and `check` with beautiful human output and JSON.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared host-catalog region engine extracted from notebooks[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog-engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog-engine: extract the notebook catalog's owned-callout region, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]host planning, and guarded sync transaction into a shared engine [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parameterized by callout name, heading, head title, and placement, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keeping every notebook byte and test identical, so the albums catalog [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and records index reuse it.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Records, capture, and completion read schemas from albums[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]album-records[dim] · [dim][/dim]after album-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]album-records: route all eight config call sites through the registry so[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record kinds follow `--bob-dir`, write album records as `type: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"[\\[record]]\"` under their album, teach `bob records check` the album [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]membership rules, enrich capture, capture-targets, and JSON additively [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with album identity, and make a bare album route (`Blaze @eat`) a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]teaching refusal.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The generated records index inside each album, rebuilt with [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]every record write[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]album-index[dim] · [dim][/dim]after album-records, catalog-engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]album-index: render the bob-owned `[!records]` index (tally title, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]groups in declared status order, sub-groups by `index_by`, faceted [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows), rebuild it in the same transaction as every capture or `bob [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]records` write from the album slice alone, and add `bob albums sync` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plus its nightly step.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The Albums catalog in owner notes, and bob albums create[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]album-catalog[dim] · [dim][/dim]after album-index[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]album-catalog: write one stable `[!albums]` row per album into each [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]owner's `## Albums` section on the shared engine (placed after `## [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Notebooks`), extend sync, list, and check to catalogs, protect the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section from capture, and add `bob albums create`, which also replaces [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`records init` for album kinds.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Obsidian album cards, live chips, and the album header[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]plugins-albums[dim] · [dim][/dim]after album-catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugins-albums: in bob-ledger-tools, style the `[!albums]` and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`[!records]` callouts as hue-accented cards, draw live count, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lead-group, peek, and freshness chips from `bob albums list -f json`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fold long index groups, render the album header with breadcrumb, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add-record affordance, and schema card, and run a debounced `bob albums [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture presents albums[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-albums[dim] · [dim][/dim]after album-records[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-albums: show each record route's album title, owner, and summary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from the additive capture-targets fields, render the bare-album refusal [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with its one-key `@eat/` rewrite, and name the album in record previews [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and success lines, gated on the exact-SHA macOS CI run.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Album cutover in the vault, then delete records from chezmoi[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]vault-cutover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after vault-cleanup, album-catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault-cutover: once every host runs album-aware bob, move each schema [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into its album's frontmatter under an equivalence gate, add the album [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and record type notes, merge and delete the four kind stubs, retype the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]152 records, update the Base filters, sync the indexes and catalogs, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]delete `records:` from chezmoi.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Link the spending ledger to restaurant records and backfill [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]visited[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]ledger-mining[dim] · [dim][/dim]after vault-cutover[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger-mining: when accepted, rewrite the 653 mappable `[\\[eat#<lid>]]` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]spending links in historical `_habit.md` notes to their records and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]backfill each restaurant's `visited` from its latest ledger date in one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reviewed commit; otherwise close as a no-op.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire config-declared records, end-to-end proof, docs audit,[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]and memory[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]albums-wrapup[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plugins-albums, mac-albums, vault-cutover, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]ledger-mining[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]albums-wrapup: remove the config `records:` reader and its transition [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fallback, turn `records init` into a hidden teaching refusal, walk every[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]album gesture end to end in a temporary vault, audit every album and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record doc, and publish the accepted glossary strands and decision [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-k3","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-k3.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-330c0ba22835a04fa930cad09be44aa8","started_at":"2026-11-11T09:57:59.911405+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"257587dbaeee46ed97364ff62d6426acdff174bc31e7bd5dcafece2416e88512","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-k3.2.1.2/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"f63d7ba18efa6e35eb603599e798f2e4b2f876ebef24f40f4c502dd031dd7f54","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-k3.2.1.2/meta.json","size_bytes":712},"prompt":{"digest":"04f3d14fad6babd0118e69699721766653eb313fba08015ee82375337833c9cb","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-k3.2.1.2/prompt.md","size_bytes":196},"state":{"digest":"6e6c7746c49b5dc86ef17ea95d7c23d83f4de6223f2f5450a5790c6a3ab05e8a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-k3.2.1.2/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-k3.2.1.2","local_name":"bob-cli-k3.2.1.2","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-k3.2.1","agent_clan_generation":"20261111050743","bead_id":"bob-cli-k3.2.1.2","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-k3.2.1","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-k3.2.1.2","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub","wait_for_beads":["bob-cli-k3.2.1.1"]},"source_run_id":"run-3ed66df4b466c14699564412c0111316","started_at":"20261111050744","state":"waiting"}